# Own-wording spells of Deep Magic (2014 rules), chunk h (Life Hack to Phantom Dragon). TEXT = {name: text}.
TEXT = {
"Life Hack": "Range 30 ft, 1 hour. Pick up to five creatures you can see. Together they share a pool of 120 Temporary Hit Points.\n\n**Drawing from the pool.** Each creature can draw up to 120 divided by the number of creatures sharing the pool. Drawing is a bonus action, and a creature can take any amount up to its limit at once. A creature that already has Temporary Hit Points from any source, including an earlier casting of this spell, cannot draw from the pool.",
"Life Sense": "Self, concentration not required, 10 minutes. You sense every living creature within 30 feet, even through barriers that block your other senses. Constructs, undead and dead creatures are not sensed.\n\n**Hiding.** A creature trying to mask its life force can make a Charisma save. On a success, you cannot sense it with this casting. If you cast the spell again, it must save again.",
"Life Transference Arrow": "Range 120 ft. Make a ranged spell attack against a creature you can see. On a miss, the spell fails. When you cast it, choose one of two outcomes.\n\n**Drain.** On a hit, the target takes 2d6 necrotic damage and you regain the same number of hit points.\n\n**Give.** On a hit, you take 2d6 necrotic damage and the target regains the same number of hit points.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** The damage and the healing each increase by 1d6 for each slot level above 1.",
"Life from Death": "Self, concentration, up to 1 minute. Your touch pulls life energy out of the undead. Make a melee spell attack against an undead creature within your reach. On a hit, it takes 2d6 radiant damage and either you or an ally within 30 feet regains hit points equal to half that damage.\n\n**Limits.** Healing an ally can bring it to no more than half its hit point maximum. Undead and constructs cannot be healed this way.\n\n**Each turn.** Until the spell ends, you can repeat the attack on each of your turns as an action.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** The damage increases by 1d6 for each slot level above 3.",
"Litany of Sure Hands": "Range 30 ft, 1 minute, bonus action to cast. One creature in range performs a simple task as a bonus action on each of its turns. Examples are finding an item in a pack, drinking a potion or pulling a rope. Attacking and casting spells do not count, and the GM rules on borderline cases. The target also ignores the loading property of weapons.",
"Living Shadows": "Range 120 ft, 1 minute. Choose a point you can see. Writhing shadows fill a 15-foot-radius sphere there and grasp at creatures.\n\n**Grasp.** A creature that starts its turn in the area, or enters it for the first time on its turn, makes a Strength save or is Restrained.\n\n**Drain.** A creature that starts its turn Restrained by the shadows makes a Constitution save or gains one level of Exhaustion.\n\n**Breaking free.** A Restrained creature can use its action to make a Strength or Dexterity check against your spell save DC. On a success, it frees itself.",
"Lock Armor": "Range 60 ft, concentration, up to 1 minute. Target a piece of metal equipment or a metal construct. If the target is a creature in metal armor or is a construct, it makes a Wisdom save to resist.\n\n**Locked up.** On a failed save, metal clings to metal and the parts cannot slide against each other. A creature made of metal or wearing metal armor with moving pieces is Paralyzed. Scale mail would lock because the scales must slide over each other, but a breastplate would not. Movement may stay partly possible depending on the armor, and speech is usually unaffected. The DM decides which armor qualifies.\n\n**Repeating saves.** An affected creature or construct repeats the save at the end of each of its turns and ends the effect on itself on a success. A grease spell ends this spell on everything in its area.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** You can target one additional creature for each slot level above 2.",
"Looping Trail": "Touch, 8 hours. You touch a trail up to 1 mile long and reshape it with switchbacks and curves so it loops back on itself. The trail and its surroundings shift subtly so travel seems to move forward along one continuous path. A creature on the trail must succeed on a Wisdom (Survival) check to notice it is walking a closed loop.",
"Lovesick": "Range 90 ft, concentration, up to 1 minute. Pick a point in range. Each creature in a 10-foot-radius sphere there makes a Wisdom save or is affected. An affected creature cannot take reactions and rolls a d10 at the start of each of its turns to see how it acts.\n\n**1 to 3.** It mopes and neither moves nor takes actions.\n\n**4 or 5.** It bursts into tears, takes the Dash action and spends all its movement running in a random direction. Roll a d8 for the direction.\n\n**6.** It uses its action to remove a piece of clothing or armor. Each round spent removing armor lowers its AC by 1.\n\n**7 or 8.** It drops what it holds and embraces a random creature. Treat this as a grapple attempt made with the Attack action.\n\n**9.** It flies into a jealous rage and uses its action to make a melee attack against a random creature.\n\n**10.** It acts and moves normally.\n\n**Repeating saves.** At the end of each of its turns, an affected creature makes a Wisdom save and ends the effect on itself on a success.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** The sphere's radius increases by 5 feet for each slot level above 4.",
"Lower the Veil": "Range 60 ft. You briefly lift the veil of reality and let the void beyond break minds. Each creature you choose within 60 feet of you makes a Wisdom save.\n\n**Failure.** The creature takes 8d10 psychic damage and is driven insane for 10 minutes, as with the symbol spell.\n\n**Success.** The creature takes half damage and is Stunned for 1 round.\n\n**Exceptions.** Creatures already suffering from insanity are immune. Blindness gives no protection because the effect is an inner awareness and not sight.",
"Machine Sacrifice": "Touch, 1 minute. You sacrifice a willing construct you can see to give a willing target the traits of a construct. The target gains resistance to all nonmagical damage and immunity to the Blinded, Charmed, Deafened, Frightened, Petrified and Poisoned conditions.",
"Machine Speech": "Self, 1 round. Your voice and, to a lesser degree, your mind shift into the whirring clicks of machine speech. Until the end of your next turn, each clockwork spell you cast has Advantage on its attack rolls, or its targets have Disadvantage on their saving throws.",
"Machine's Load": "Touch, concentration, up to 1 minute. A creature you touch can carry, lift, push and drag weight as if it were one size larger. If you use encumbrance rules, it takes no penalties for weight. It can also carry loads that would normally be unwieldy.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** You can touch one additional creature for each slot level above 1.",
"Maddening Whispers": "Range 30 ft, 1 minute. You whisper Void Speech at a target that can hear you. It makes a Charisma save or is Incapacitated. While Incapacitated this way, its Speed is 0 and it cannot gain any increase to its Speed.\n\n**Keeping it going.** You must use your action on each later turn to keep whispering, or the spell ends. The spell also ends if the target takes damage.",
"Magma Spray": "Range 40 ft, concentration, up to 1 minute. A cylinder of magma, 5 feet across and 5 feet tall, erupts from the ground in a space you choose in range.\n\n**Damage.** A creature in that space takes 3d8 fire damage, or half on a successful Dexterity save. A creature that enters the space on its turn or ends its turn there takes the same damage and gets the same save. A creature takes this damage only once per turn.\n\n**Ash.** A creature reduced to 0 hit points by this damage dies at once and its body burns to ash.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** The damage increases by 1d8 for each slot level above 2.",
"Magnetize": "Touch, 10 minutes. You magnetize a large piece of metal or stone you touch, such as a door, a pillar or a 5-foot square of floor. It strongly attracts ferrous metal.\n\n**Pull.** Iron objects within 50 feet that are not fastened down, held or worn move toward the target and stay stuck to it. A creature standing between an object and the magnet may be struck. Make a ranged spell attack against its AC. On a hit, it takes 2d10 damage of the fitting type, such as bludgeoning for a hammer or slashing or piercing for a sword.\n\n**Held and worn items.** A creature must succeed on a Strength save to keep hold of held or worn objects. On a success, it keeps them but is dragged 5 feet closer to the magnet. A creature can choose to let go of a metal item and skip the save.\n\n**Metal creatures.** Creatures made of metal or wearing mostly metal armor are pulled too and have Disadvantage on their saves. On a success, such a creature can move away from the magnet on its turn. The area within 50 feet is difficult terrain. If the creature is still in it at the start of its next turn, it must save again or be drawn in.\n\n**Contact.** A creature touching the magnet is Restrained. It can end this by using an action and succeeding on a Strength check against your spell save DC.",
"Maim": "Self, instant. Your hands become black claws wreathed in necrotic energy. Make a melee spell attack against a creature you can reach. On a hit, it takes 4d6 necrotic damage and one part of its body that you choose withers.\n\n**Upper Limb.** The target has Disadvantage on Strength checks. If it has the Multiattack action, it has Disadvantage on its first attack roll each round.\n\n**Lower Limb.** The target's Speed is reduced by 10 feet and it has Disadvantage on Dexterity checks.\n\n**Body.** Choose bludgeoning, piercing or slashing damage. The target loses any resistance to that type. If it had no resistance, it becomes vulnerable to that type.\n\n**Duration.** The effect lasts until ended by remove curse, greater restoration or similar magic.",
"Malevolent Waves": "Self, 1 minute. You fill the area within 30 feet of you with an invisible miasma. Your allies have Advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks while within 30 feet of you. Your enemies are Poisoned while within that distance.",
"Mammon's Avarice": "Range 30 ft, 10 minutes. You tap into greed and gain a sharpened sense of smell for wealth. You can pinpoint any precious metals or gemstones within 30 feet. If you find some, you can use an action to learn their exact types and amounts.\n\n**Blocked.** You cannot detect materials fully enclosed by, or separated from you by, more than 6 feet of earth or wood, 2 feet of stone or 2 inches of common metal.",
"Mammon's Due": "Range 500 ft, concentration, up to 1 minute. You open a cylindrical sinkhole, 20 feet deep and 50 feet across, at a point on the ground you can see. It is filled with burning ash and grasping arms of molten metal, and it is difficult terrain.\n\n**Burning.** A creature that is in the area when you cast the spell, or that starts its turn there or enters it during its turn, takes 10d6 fire damage and makes a Strength or Dexterity save (its choice). On a failure, the arms Restrain it and try to drag it under.\n\n**Dragged under.** A creature Restrained by the arms at the start of your turn must succeed on a Strength save or be pulled 5 feet deeper. A creature pulled below the surface is Blinded, Deafened and cannot breathe.\n\n**Escape.** A creature can use an action to make a Strength or Dexterity check against your spell save DC. On a success, it is no longer Restrained and can move through the ash as difficult terrain. It does not need to save against being grabbed again this turn, but it saves as normal if it is still in the pit at the start of its next turn.\n\n**Growth.** The pit's diameter grows by 10 feet at the start of each of your turns while the spell lasts.\n\n**Afterward.** The pit stays when the spell ends, but the arms vanish and free any restrained creatures. As the ash cools, it deals 1d6 less fire damage for each hour that passes after the spell ends.",
"Mantle of the Brave": "Touch, 1 hour. You bolster up to four creatures you touch. The next time an affected creature must make a saving throw against a spell or effect that would make it Frightened, it has Advantage on the save. After a creature gets this benefit, the spell ends for it.",
"Mark Prey": "Range 120 ft, concentration, up to 1 hour, bonus action to cast. Choose a creature you can see in range as your prey.\n\n**Tracking.** You have Advantage on Wisdom (Perception) and Wisdom (Survival) checks to find or follow your prey.\n\n**Outline.** Light that only you can see outlines the target. You have Advantage on attack rolls against your prey if you can see it, and it gains no benefit from being invisible against you.\n\n**New prey.** If the target drops to 0 hit points before the spell ends, you can use a bonus action on a later turn to mark a new target.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** With a 4th-level slot, you can concentrate for up to 8 hours. With a 5th-level slot or higher, you can concentrate for up to 24 hours.",
"Mass Blade Ward": "Range 30 ft, 1 round. Choose three creatures you can see in range. Until the end of your next turn, they have resistance to bludgeoning, piercing and slashing damage from weapon attacks. The effect ends for a creature that moves more than 30 feet from you.",
"Mass Hobble Mount": "Range 60 ft, concentration, up to 1 hour. Make a separate ranged spell attack against each of up to six beasts being ridden as mounts within 60 feet of you, such as horses, wolves or other two or four legged beasts. They can be of different kinds.\n\n**Hobbled.** A beast you hit is disabled so that it cannot move at its normal speed without being hurt. If an affected creature moves more than half its base speed in a turn, it takes 4d6 bludgeoning damage.\n\n**Limit.** The spell has no effect on a creature the GM does not consider a mount.",
"Mass Repair Metal": "Range 60 ft radius, instant. This works like repair metal, but you can affect all metal in range. You mend rents and bend metal back into place, repairing 1d8 + 5 damage on each metal object or construct.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** Cast as a 6th-level spell, it repairs 2d8 + 10 damage.",
"Mass Surge Dampener": "Range 30 ft, 1 minute, ritual. You shield up to three creatures other than yourself from chaos magic surges.\n\n**Protection.** A protected creature can make a DC 13 Charisma save to negate a chaos magic surge that normally allows no save. Against a surge that does allow a save, it has Advantage.\n\n**Ending.** After a protected creature makes a successful save that this spell affected, the spell ends for that creature.",
"Maw of Needles": "Self, 1 minute, bonus action to cast. Needle-like fangs grow in your mouth and give you a spiny bite. For the duration, you can use your action to make a melee spell attack with it.\n\n**Bite.** On a hit, the target takes 2d6 piercing damage and makes a Dexterity save. On a failure, spines break off and stick in it.\n\n**Spines.** Until the spell ends, the stuck target makes a Constitution save at the start of each of its turns or takes 1d6 piercing damage. When you hit a target that has your spines in it, your attack deals extra damage equal to your spellcasting ability modifier, and no more spines break off.\n\n**One at a time.** Your spines can be stuck in only one target. If they stick in another, the earlier spines crumble to dust and that effect ends.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** The damage of the bite and of the spines each increases by 1d6 for every two slot levels above 1.",
"Mechanical Union": "Range 60 ft, concentration, up to 1 hour. You take control of a construct with voice or mental commands. The construct makes a Wisdom save to resist, with Advantage if its CR equals or exceeds your level in the class you used to cast this spell.\n\n**Obedience.** Once given a command, the construct does everything it can to carry it out. Giving a new command takes an action. It will risk harm and even fight on your orders, but it will not destroy itself. An order to do so ends the spell.",
"Memento Mori": "Self, 5 ft, 1 round. You turn yourself into a horrifying vision of death, rotting and crawling with maggots and reeking of the grave. Each creature within 5 feet that can see you makes a Charisma save or is Stunned until the end of its next turn. A creature that succeeds is immune to further castings of this spell for 24 hours.",
"Memento Mori ": "",
"Mephitic Croak": "15-foot cone, instant. You release a deafening burp of acidic gas. Each creature in the cone takes 2d6 acid damage plus 2d6 thunder damage, or half as much on a successful Dexterity save.\n\n**Stun.** A creature that fails the Dexterity save also makes a Constitution save. On a failure, it is Stunned and Poisoned until the start of your next turn.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** Both the acid damage and the thunder damage increase by 1d6 for each slot level above 2.",
"Mind Exchange": "Range 60 ft, concentration, up to 8 hours, 1 minute to cast, ritual. One humanoid you can see in range makes a Charisma save. On a failure, your mind moves into its body and its mind moves into yours.\n\n**Swapped.** You use the target's statistics but keep your own knowledge, class features and proficiencies. The target does the reverse with your body, using your statistics and keeping its own knowledge, class features and proficiencies.\n\n**Ending.** The exchange lasts until one of the two bodies drops to 0 hit points, until you end it as a bonus action, or until an effect such as dispel magic or dispel evil and good forces you out. Dispel evil and good ends this spell even though it does not normally affect possession by a humanoid. When it ends, both minds return to their own bodies.\n\n**Immunity.** The target is immune to this spell for 24 hours after it succeeds on the save or after the exchange ends.\n\n**Permanence.** A wish spell or similar magic can make the exchange permanent.",
"Mire": "Range 100 ft, 1 hour. You create a pit of quicksand, sticky mud or a similar natural hazard that fits the region. It is 10 feet across.\n\n**Sinking.** A creature in the area when you cast the spell, or one that enters it, makes a Strength save or sinks to its waist and is Restrained. From then on, the mire works as quicksand, but the DC of Strength checks to escape it equals your spell save DC.\n\n**Help.** A creature outside the mire that tries to pull another creature free gets a +5 bonus to its Strength check.",
"Misfortune": "Range 60 ft, concentration, up to 1 minute. You lay a pall of bad luck over all creatures in a 15-foot radius around a point in range. Each creature in the area makes a Wisdom save or is cursed with bad luck for the duration. A cursed creature has Disadvantage on all ability checks, saving throws and attack rolls. Remove curse ends the effect.\n\n**Lucky items.** A targeted creature carrying a stone of good luck is unaffected, but the item stops working for 24 hours. A targeted creature carrying a luck blade is also unaffected, but the sword's Luck ability and saving throw bonuses stop working for 24 hours.",
"Misstep": "Range 30 ft, instant. You gesture at a creature you can see in range. If it fails a Wisdom save, it uses its reaction to move 5 feet in a direction you choose. This movement does not provoke opportunity attacks.\n\n**Limits.** The spell fails automatically if you direct the target into a dangerous spot such as a pit trap, a bonfire or off a cliff edge, or if the target has already used its reaction.",
"Mist of Wonders": "Self, 30 ft radius, 1 minute. A colorful mist surrounds you out to 30 feet. Creatures inside see odd shapes and hear random sounds, and order and logic seem not to exist there.\n\n**Warped spells.** A 1st-level spell cast inside the mist by another caster, or that passes through it, is altered. The caster makes a Constitution save when casting. On a failure, the spell turns into another 1st-level spell the caster knows, chosen by the GM, even if that spell is not prepared. The slot level, original target and original area cannot change. Cantrips are unaffected. If the GM judges that none of the caster's known spells of that level can serve, the spell simply fails.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** With a 3rd-level slot or higher, the mist affects any spell cast with a slot of a lower level. For example, a 6th-level slot lets you transform a spell of 5th level or lower into another spell of the same level.",
"Mithral Dragon's Might": "Self, concentration, up to 1 minute. You take on traits of a mithral dragon and grow protective scales, wings and claws.\n\n**Scales.** Your AC cannot be lower than 16 whatever armor you wear. You have resistance to acid and thunder damage.\n\n**Claws.** You can use your action to attack twice with your claws. Each hit deals 1d6 slashing damage plus your spellcasting ability modifier.\n\n**Wings.** You gain a flying speed of 40 feet.\n\n**Breath.** Up to three times while the spell lasts, you can use an action to breathe a 20-foot cone of metal shards. Each creature in the cone takes 6d8 slashing damage, or half as much on a successful Dexterity save.",
"Molech's Blessing": "Touch, instant, 1 hour ritual begun at midnight. You dedicate a living being to the furnace god Molech by branding his symbol on its forehead. When the ritual is finished, the victim makes a Wisdom save, or chooses not to. On a failure, it becomes an avatar of Molech under your control.\n\n**The avatar.** It stands 8 feet tall and looks like black iron wreathed in flames, with its eyes, mouth and part of its torso cut away to show churning fire and wailing voices. It uses the statistics and abilities of an earth elemental, with these differences. Its alignment is Neutral Evil. Its Speed is 50 feet and it cannot burrow or use earth glide. It gains the fire form ability of a fire elemental but cannot squeeze through small spaces. Its Slam deals an extra 1d10 fire damage.\n\n**Ending.** The transformation lasts 24 hours. Then the subject returns to normal and takes 77 (14d10) fire damage, or half as much on a successful DC 15 Constitution save.",
"Monstrous Empathy": "Range 30 ft, 24 hours. Choose a monstrosity you can see in range. It must be able to see and hear you. If its Intelligence is 4 or higher, the spell fails. Otherwise it makes a Wisdom save or is Charmed by you for the duration. The spell ends if you or one of your companions harms the target.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** You can affect one additional monstrosity for each slot level above 3.",
"Moon Trap": "Self, up to 8 hours. You must cast this under moonlight. You inscribe a glyph that covers a 10-foot square on a flat, stationary surface such as a floor or wall. When the spell is complete, the glyph is invisible in moonlight and glows faintly white in darkness.\n\n**Trap.** A creature that touches the glyph, other than those you name when casting, makes a Wisdom save or is drawn into an inescapable maze until the sun rises.\n\n**Release.** The glyph lasts until the next sunrise, when it flares with bright light. Trapped creatures return unharmed to the space they last occupied. If that space is occupied or dangerous, a creature appears in the nearest safe unoccupied space.",
"Moonlight Charm": "Range 30 ft, up to 4 weeks. You try to charm a humanoid you can see in range. It makes a Wisdom save, with Advantage if you or your companions are fighting or threatening it.\n\n**Charmed.** On a failed save, the humanoid is Charmed until the duration ends, until you or a companion does anything harmful to it, or until a full moon rises. It regards you as a friendly acquaintance. When the spell ends, it knows you charmed it.",
"Mortal Insight": "Self, concentration, up to 10 minutes. You gain a supernatural sense of smell for wounded living creatures. You can pinpoint any creature within 30 feet that is missing hit points. You have Advantage on Wisdom (Perception) and Wisdom (Survival) checks to track such a creature, and Advantage on melee attack rolls against it.\n\n**Limit.** The spell has no effect on creatures that have no blood.",
"Mosquito Bane": "Range 50 ft, instant. This spell kills every insect and insect swarm in range that has 25 hit points or fewer in total.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** The hit point limit increases by 15 for each slot level above 1. A 2nd-level slot kills those with up to 40 hit points, a 3rd-level slot up to 55, and so on, to a maximum of 85 hit points with a slot of 6th level or higher.",
"Move the Cosmic Wheel": "Range 120 ft, 24 hours. You wind your music box and call forth a piece of another plane that you know through personal experience or intense study. A bubble of space with a 30-foot radius appears in range at a spot you choose. The part of your plane inside the bubble swaps places with the matching part of the plane your music box is attuned to.\n\n**Natives.** There is a 10 percent chance that the arriving piece comes with native creatures on it.\n\n**Edges.** Objects and non-moving life such as trees are cut off at the bubble's edge. Living creatures that do not fit inside are pushed outside before the swap.\n\n**Creatures caught inside.** Creatures from both planes inside the bubble go with their piece of reality to the other plane for the duration, unless they make a Charisma save when the spell is cast. On a success, a creature chooses whether to switch planes with the bubble or leap out a moment before the swap.\n\n**Interaction.** Natural reactions between the two planes occur normally, so fire spreads and water glows. Energy such as necrotic energy leaks slowly across the edge, no more than a foot or two per hour. Otherwise creatures and effects move freely across the boundary. For the duration, the bubble becomes part of its new location as fully as the two planes allow.\n\n**Return.** The two displaced bubbles shift back after 24 hours.\n\n**Note.** The preparation needed to acquire and attune the music box rules out casting this on the spur of the moment. Its effects are unpredictable and wide-ranging, so talk with your GM before adding it to your spells.",
"Mud Pack": "Touch, 1 hour. You coat yourself or a willing creature you touch in mud that matches the local terrain. The target is protected from extreme cold and heat and automatically succeeds on Constitution saves against temperature hazards. It also has Advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks while traveling at a slow pace in the terrain tied to the spell's component.\n\n**Rain.** If the target is in heavy precipitation for 1 minute, the rain washes off the mud and the spell ends.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** With a 3rd-level slot or higher, the duration is 8 hours and you can target up to ten willing creatures within 30 feet of you.",
"Nature's Aegis": "Self, 1 hour. Grass, vines, branches and other plants weave over your body into a temporary suit of armor. The armor weighs 8 pounds and gives you AC 14 + your Dexterity modifier. You also have Advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks to hide in the terrain that the plants came from. You can use an action to dismiss the spell, and the armor then falls apart into plain vegetation.",
"Necrotic Leech": "Touch, instant. You channel destructive energy through your touch. Make a melee spell attack against a creature within your reach. On a hit, it takes 8d10 necrotic damage and makes a Constitution save. On a failure, it has Disadvantage on attack rolls, saving throws and ability checks for a number of rounds equal to the level of the slot you used.\n\n**Repeating saves.** The creature repeats the save at the end of each of its turns and ends the effect on itself on a success.\n\n**Limit.** The spell has no effect on constructs or undead.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** The damage increases by 1d10 for each slot level above 5.",
"Negative Image": "Range 120 ft, instant. You create a shadow tunnel between you and one other creature you can see in range. You and that creature instantly swap positions. An unwilling target can make a Charisma save. On a success, the spell has no effect.",
"Nest of Infernal Vipers": "Range 60 ft, concentration, up to 1 hour. You summon evil spirits in the form of a swarm of poisonous snakes in an unoccupied space you can see in range. The swarm counts as a fiend as well as a beast and has resistance to fire damage. It lasts until it drops to 0 hit points or the spell ends.\n\n**Control.** The swarm is friendly to you and your companions and rolls its own initiative. It obeys your verbal commands with no action from you. With no commands, it moves to attack the nearest creature that is not your ally. The GM has its statistics.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** You summon two swarms with a 5th-level slot, three with a 7th-level slot, and four with a 9th-level slot.",
"Nether Weapon": "Touch, concentration, up to 1 hour. You whisper in Void Speech and touch a weapon. The weapon turns black and becomes magical if it was not already. On a hit, it deals an extra 2d6 necrotic damage. A creature that takes this necrotic damage cannot regain hit points until the start of your next turn.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** The extra damage increases by 1d6 for each slot level above 4.",
"Night Terrors": "Range 120 ft, concentration, up to 1 minute. You amplify the fear in every heart. Choose a point you can see in range. Every creature within 20 feet of it is Frightened until the start of your next turn and must make a Wisdom save or be Paralyzed.\n\n**Repeating saves.** A Paralyzed creature repeats the save at the end of each of its turns and ends the effect on itself on a success.\n\n**Immunity.** Creatures immune to being Frightened are not affected.",
"Nightfall": "Range 100 ft, concentration, up to 1 minute. With a sharp word, you call night early. You create a cylinder of night with a 30-foot radius centered on a point on the ground in range. It rises 100 feet or until it meets an obstruction such as a ceiling. The inside is normal darkness, so it is heavily obscured. Creatures inside can see lit areas outside the cylinder normally.",
"Nimbleness": "Touch, concentration, up to 1 minute. A willing creature you touch can, once before the spell ends, roll a d6 and add it to one Dexterity check of its choice. It can roll before or after the check. The spell then ends.",
"Nip at the Heels": "Range 30 ft, 1 minute. You create an illusory pack of wild dogs that bark and nip at one creature you can see in range. The target makes a Wisdom save. On a failure, it has Disadvantage on ability checks and attack rolls for the duration, distracted by the dogs.\n\n**Repeating saves.** At the end of each of its turns, the target makes a Wisdom save and ends the effect on itself on a success.\n\n**Out of reach.** A target at least 10 feet off the ground, such as in a tree or flying, has Advantage on the save because it stays beyond the leaping dogs.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** You can target one additional creature for each slot level above 2.",
"Not Dead Yet": "Touch, concentration, up to 1 hour. You cast this while touching a cloth doll to the intact corpse of a Medium or smaller humanoid that died within the last hour. At the end of the casting, the body rises as an undead creature under your control. Your consciousness moves into it while your own body falls Unconscious.\n\n**Using the body.** You can use an action to move its limbs, and you see and hear through its eyes and ears. It can neither attack nor defend itself. The spell does not change the corpse's appearance, so you may need other measures to fool observers. You can use none of its abilities except nonmagical movement and darkvision. You have no access to its knowledge or proficiencies, and you cannot make it speak.\n\n**Ending.** The spell ends at once, and your mind returns to your body, if either your real body or the animated body takes any damage.",
"Not This Day!": "Touch, 24 hours. The creature you touch gains protection against one damage type, such as slashing, poison, fire or radiant, or against one category of creature, such as giant, beast, elemental or monstrosity. You name it when you cast the spell.\n\n**Protection.** For 24 hours, the target has Advantage on saving throws involving that damage type or creature kind. This includes death saving throws if the attack that dropped it to 0 hit points was covered by the spell.\n\n**One at a time.** A character can be under only one casting of this spell. A second casting on the same target cancels the earlier protection.",
"Nourishing Repast": "Touch, 24 hours. You touch a supply of food and turn it into a magical substance that aids healing and health. Enough food for up to six creatures can be changed. The effect lasts 24 hours or until the food is eaten.\n\n**Short rest.** If the food is eaten during a short rest, each Hit Die spent to regain hit points gains a +1 bonus.\n\n**Long rest.** If it is eaten as part of a long rest, each creature that shares the meal has Advantage on saving throws against disease and poison for the next 8 hours.",
"Obtuse": "Range 30 ft, 1 minute. You cloud the mind of a creature in range. If it succeeds on a Wisdom save, the spell does nothing. On a failure, the next time it makes a Wisdom check before the spell ends, it rolls a d6 and subtracts the result from the check. The spell then ends.",
"Opportunistic Foresight": "Touch, concentration, up to 1 minute. You give a creature you touch the ability to predict openings in combat. For the duration, the target gains a bonus action on each of its turns that it can use to make an opportunity attack against a provoking opponent. It also has Advantage on any opportunity attack it makes while the spell lasts.",
"Orb of Light": "Range 60 ft, 1 round. An orb of light the size of your hand shoots from your fingertips at a creature in range. The target takes 3d8 radiant damage and is Blinded for 1 round. On a successful Dexterity save, it takes half damage and is not Blinded.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** The damage increases by 1d8 for each slot level above 2.",
"Outflanking Boon": "Range 30 ft, concentration, up to 1 minute. You target one enemy, which makes a Wisdom save. On a failure, an illusory ally of yours appears in a space from which it threatens to attack the target in melee. The illusion distracts the target, so your allies have Advantage on melee attacks against it for the duration.\n\n**Repeating saves.** The target repeats the save at the end of each of its turns and ends the effect on itself on a success.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** The spell targets one additional enemy for each slot level above 3.",
"Overclock": "Range 30 ft, concentration, up to 1 minute. You make a piece of clockwork speed up past the point of control. The target cannot cast spells with verbal components or communicate well, since its words sound like grinding gears.\n\n**Each turn.** At the start of each of its turns, the target makes a Wisdom save. On a failure, it moves at three times its normal speed in a random direction and its turn ends, and it can do nothing else. On a success, its speed is doubled until the end of its turn and it gains an additional action. That action must be Attack (one weapon attack only), Dash, Disengage, Hide or Use an Object.\n\n**Ending.** When the spell ends, the clockwork takes 2d8 force damage.",
"Overwhelming Greed": "Range 60 ft, 1 hour. You fill the target with a dragon's greed for wealth. It makes a Wisdom save or is overcome with greed. It covets any coins, jewelry or art objects it can see that are worth at least 1 gp, and it jealously guards the wealth it already owns. It fixates on the most valuable-looking item or items, or on the largest pile of valuables in sight, and will not willingly let that wealth out of its sight. If it sees an opening, it takes what it fixated on by any means necessary.\n\n**Harm.** If this causes it to take damage or be otherwise harmed, it can make another Wisdom save to end the effect. If it fails, it keeps trying to get the wealth and fights back if needed.\n\n**Ending the effect.** If the creature ends its turn where it can see no obviously valuable objects to covet and no creatures that might try to take its own property, it can make another Wisdom save. A horse, for example, would not count as such a creature. A success ends the spell, and the creature knows its greed was magically induced.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** You can affect one additional creature for each slot level above 4.",
"Paragon of Chaos": "Self, concentration, up to 1 minute. You become a humanoid-shaped swirl of color and sound.\n\n**Defenses.** You gain resistance to bludgeoning, piercing and slashing damage, and immunity to poison and psychic damage. You are immune to the Exhaustion, Paralyzed, Petrified, Poisoned and Unconscious conditions.\n\n**Senses and movement.** You gain truesight to 30 feet and can teleport 30 feet as part of your move.\n\n**Surges.** Each round, as a bonus action, you can trigger a chaos magic surge. You choose yourself or another creature you can see within 60 feet as the caster for resolving the effect. You must choose the target before you roll the percentile dice to determine the surge. Any save DC is figured as if you were the caster.",
"Pendulum": "Touch, concentration, up to 1 minute. You give a creature you touch a regularity in its motions and fortunes. If the target fails a Wisdom save, then for the duration it does not roll d20s. For attack rolls, ability checks and saving throws, it instead follows the sequence 20, 1, 19, 2, 18, 3, 17, 4 and so on.",
"Phantom Dragon": "Touch, concentration, up to 1 hour. You tap dragon magic to make an ally look like a draconic beast. The target appears to be a dragon of Large size or smaller. When observers first see the illusion, they make a Wisdom save to see through it.\n\n**Ferocity.** You can use an action to make the illusory dragon look ferocious. Choose one creature within 30 feet of it, which makes a Wisdom save or is Frightened. It stays Frightened until it uses an action to make a successful Wisdom save or the duration ends.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** The illusion can affect one more target for each slot level above 3.",
}
